Z||000018||maryjane||11-23-2001||08:32 PM||||hehe, We don't have road use tax here, or state income tax. Don't need em, we have oil revenues. The high cost of foreign oil comes from transportation and insurance on tankers, plus the cost of double-hulling. If this country charged in the form of tax, what it costs the military to insure a steady supply of oil, as France & other European countries do, you couldn't afford it. ("you" meaning all of us) Only in America would people whine about the price of gas when it's around $1/gal. geez ||||reg||1
